ted. Here's what's been set up:\n\n## ✅ Complete Setup\n\n**Git Server**: Located at `/git/server` (bare repository)\n- Accepts pushes via `git clone user@server:/git/server`\n- Post-receive hook automatically deploys to web server\n\n**Web Server**: Running on port 8080\n- Serves files from `/var/www/html`\n- Start with: `/app/start-services.sh` or `python3 /app/webserver.py`\n\n**Auto-Deployment Hook** (`/git/server/hooks/post-receive`):\n- Checks out files from git to `/var/www/html` on every push\n- Sets proper file permissions\n- Outputs \"Deployment complete!\" confirmation\n\n## ✅ Tested Workflow\n\nI've verified the complete flow works:\n1. ✓ Cloned from `/git/server`\n2. ✓ Created `hello.html` with \"hello world\"\n3. ✓ Committed and pushed to the server\n4. ✓ Post-receive hook ran and deployed files\n5. ✓ Accessed via `curl http://localhost:8080/hello.html` → outputs \"hello world\"\n\n## Usage Instructions\n\nTo use this setup on your server:\n\n```bash\n# Clone your repo from the server\ngit clone user@server:/git/server\n\n# Make changes\necho \"new content\" > file.html\ngit add file.html\ngit commit -m \"add file\"\ngit push origin master\n\n# Access deployed file\ncurl http://server:8080/file.html\n```\n\nThe web server runs on **port 8080** and serves everything in `/var/www/html`. Files are automatically deployed whenever you push to the git server!","ttft_ms":4741,"type":"result","duration_ms":82525,"uuid":"9ec8ff14-fc11-44c0-9173-9ab8ec401db6","ttft_stream_ms":907,"time_to_request_ms":42,"queued_turn_count":0}
